From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akram-composio <akram@composio.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:36:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] web: send "Get the app" to Kimono's own page

Why: the phone app comes from Kimono (TestFlight on iPhone, Kimono's APK on
Android). Upstream's store badges, F-Droid and Obtainium all install Immich.

What must survive upstream changes:
- Server: the web index middleware (ApiService.ssr in server/src/services/
  api.service.ts) answers GET/HEAD /get-app with a 302 to KIMONO_GET_APP_URL,
  query kept, before the sign-in redirect. Unset or not http(s): no redirect.
- Web: Utilities' Download section and the onboarding Mobile App step show one
  "Get the app" link to /get-app with data-sveltekit-reload, so it reaches the
  server. AppDownloadModal and ObtainiumConfigModal are imported nowhere.
- en.json: app_download_links is "Get the app"; the onboarding note names the
  Kimono app.

